From 34fa9974a1eaf709e17fc28af415aa45f0a4cd94 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anton Protopopov <a.s.protopopov@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 17:36:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] bpf: Allow BPF_OBJ_GET in bpf_sys_bpf()

A loader generated by the gen_loader creates maps and loads programs
from the kernel, but can't use an object pinned before it ran. This
limits what a light skeleton can load. For example, a program which
attaches to another BPF program via freplace or fentry/fexit needs
the target's fd at load time, and the loader has no way to obtain it.

Now that the BPF_OBJ_GET accepts a kernel pathname, allow it in the
bpf_sys_bpf() helper. A loader can then open the target by its pin
path, a string stored in the loader's data. Unlike a program ID, which
is only known at run time, the path can be a part of the signed data,
so signed loaders can find existing BPF programs this way.

Signed-off-by: Anton Protopopov <a.s.protopopov@gmail.com>
---
 kernel/bpf/syscall.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/kernel/bpf/syscall.c b/kernel/bpf/syscall.c
index 3872bd5ee696..3a8cb7255e6a 100644
--- a/kernel/bpf/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/bpf/syscall.c
@@ -6609,6 +6609,7 @@ BPF_CALL_3(bpf_sys_bpf, int, cmd, union bpf_attr *, attr, u32, attr_size)
 	case BPF_BTF_LOAD:
 	case BPF_LINK_CREATE:
 	case BPF_RAW_TRACEPOINT_OPEN:
+	case BPF_OBJ_GET:
 		break;
 	default:
 		return -EINVAL;
